  #line-at(68.52pt, 320.52pt, "Abstract ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.345pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(68.52pt, 338.88pt, "In this work, we analyse the reverse current mechanisms in GaN Schottky barrier diodes ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 350.52pt, "(SBDs) grown on sapphire and native GaN substrates. For the sapphire-substrate sample, two ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 362.04pt, "conduction mechanisms are identified: Poole–Frenkel emission (PFE) and trap-assisted ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 373.8pt, "tunneling (TAT), with corresponding trap energy levels of 0.9 eV and 0.3 eV, respectively. In ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 385.44pt, "contrast, only PFE is observed in the GaN-substrate sample, with a trap energy of 0.75 eV, ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 397.2pt, "suggesting that the presence of TAT is related to the higher dislocation density in structures ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 408.84pt, "grown on sapphire substrates. The leakage mechanisms and associated trap energies are ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 420.36pt, "extracted by comparing experimental current–voltage (I–V) characteristics with a model that ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 432.12pt, "includes thermionic emission and tunneling contributions for different temperatures, from ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 443.76pt, "298K up to 443K. ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 466.8pt, "Keywords: GaN substrate, GaN Schottky, temperature, traps ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.358pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(68.52pt, 524.4pt, "1. Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.345pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.32pt, 542.64pt, "Wide bandgap (WBG) semiconductors present material ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 554.28pt, "properties that significantly improve the conventional ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 566.04pt, "technologies. Between them, we highlight gallium nitride ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 577.68pt, "(GaN) which presents a wide bandgap, high breakdown field, ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 589.44pt, "electron velocity and thermal conductivity [1]. These ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 600.96pt, "characteristics make GaN a promising candidate for high ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 612.72pt, "power, high frequency and high temperature applications. ")
  #line-at(79.32pt, 624.36pt, "Schottky diodes are widely used in frequency multipliers ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 636pt, "and mixers because of their strong non-linearity and in ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 647.76pt, "parallel, their high switching speed enables their use in fast-")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 659.28pt, "response applications [2,3]. While GaAs remains the most ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 671.04pt, "widely used technology for Schottky diodes, its limited ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 682.68pt, "thermal stability, relatively low breakdown voltage and ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 694.32pt, "modest power handling capability make GaN a strong ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 705.96pt, "candidate for more demanding applications.  GaN Schottky ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 717.6pt, "barrier diodes (SBDs) are particularly well suited for ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 514.08pt, "high-power, high-temperature and space electronics, and ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 525.6pt, "additionally benefit from the intrinsic radiation hardness of ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 537.36pt, "GaN.  ")
  #line-at(321.84pt, 549pt, "Reverse leakage current in GaN SBDs is comonly higher ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 560.76pt, "than that expected from thermionic and tunnel currents [4]. ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 572.4pt, "This excess current is generally associated with the presence ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 583.92pt, "of defects. The reverse current is often attributed to defect-")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 595.68pt, "assisted mechanisms such as Poole Frenkel emission (PFE), ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 607.32pt, "trap assisted tunneling (TAT), and variable range hopping ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 619.08pt, "(VRH) [5-6]. As a consequence, device reliability remains a ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 630.72pt, "key challenge that must be thoroughly investigated, as it is a ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 642.24pt, "critical requirement for applications such as space, medical, ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 654pt, "and security systems, where stable and long term operation is ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 665.64pt, "essential. ")
  #line-at(321.84pt, 677.4pt, "The lack of native GaN substrates has promoted the use of ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 689.04pt, "foreign substrates such as Si, SiC or sapphire. Although GaN ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 700.68pt, "layers grown on sapphire and SiC substrates exhibit a high ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 712.32pt, "dislocation density, typically ranging from 10⁷ to 10⁹ cm⁻², ")
]

