  #line-at(79.32pt, 75.48pt, "I-V measurements have been carried out at different ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 87.12pt, "temperatures, from 25ºC up to 170ºC by using a homemade ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 98.76pt, "experimental setup. The experimental setup consists of a ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 110.4pt, "power supply used to apply a voltage to a ceramic heater ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 122.04pt, "mounted beneath a metallic chuck, which serves as a heated ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 133.8pt, "sample holder. The temperature of the holder is monitored ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 145.44pt, "using an Agilent 34461A digital multimeter connected to a ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 157.08pt, "temperature sensor placed directly on the metallic chuck. ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 168.72pt, "Electrical probing is performed using tungsten probe tips, ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 180.48pt, "chosen for their thermal and mechanical stability under high ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 192.12pt, "temperature conditions. ")
  #line-at(79.32pt, 584.76pt, "Figure 3 shows the forward I-V characteristics for (a) ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 596.52pt, "sapphire-substrate and (b) GaN-substrate, jointly with the ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 608.16pt, "results of the model developed in Ref. [12]. The model ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 619.68pt, "considers only the thermionic emission in forward bias while ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 631.44pt, "in reverse bias we take into account the thermionic and ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 643.08pt, "tunneling currents. The derivation of the expressions used to ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 654.84pt, "calculate these currents is detailed in Ref. [12]. ")
  #line-at(79.32pt, 666.48pt, " The values of ϕ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(141.6pt, 667.32pt, "B")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.345pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(145.68pt, 666.48pt, " and η have been extracted by fitting the ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 678.12pt, "experimental curves and the ideal current obtained from the ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 689.76pt, "model. We observe in the insets of figure 3 that, for both ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 75.48pt, "samples, the ideality factor decreases while the barrier height ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 87.12pt, "increases with increasing temperature. This behavior is ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 98.76pt, "typically attributed to Schottky barrier inhomogeneities ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 110.4pt, "[13,14]. ")
  #line-at(321.84pt, 494.52pt, "Figure 4 represents the reverse I–V characteristics obtained ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 506.16pt, "from both experimental measurements and the model. For the ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 517.92pt, "diode fabricated on a sapphire substrate, a significant ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 529.44pt, "difference between the measured current and the ideal current ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 541.08pt, "is observed over the entire temperature range. In contrast, for ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 552.84pt, "the GaN-substrate sample, the experimental curves approach ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 564.48pt, "the ideal current at the highest temperatures.  ")
  #line-at(321.84pt, 576.24pt, "As we have previously mentioned, the reverse ideal current ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 587.76pt, "is estimated by the thermionic and tunneling contributions. ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 599.52pt, "The deviation from the ideal current indicates the presence of ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 611.16pt, "non-ideal current mechanisms. This deviation is more ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 622.8pt, "pronounced for the sapphire-substrate sample, and the ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 634.56pt, "difference between the measured current and the ideal current ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 646.08pt, "determines the excess current associated with non-ideal ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 657.84pt, "mechanisms. ")
  #line-at(321.84pt, 669.48pt, "The excess of current is used to identify the additional ")
  #line-at(311.04pt, 681.12pt, "mechanisms present in each structure. By representing ")
