  #line-at(68.52pt, 75.48pt, "substrate, the dislocation density is much higher (10")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(271.2pt, 72.24pt, "7")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.345pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(274.2pt, 75.48pt, " to 10")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(297.48pt, 72.24pt, "9")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.345pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(68.52pt, 87.12pt, "cm⁻²) and explains the presence of both PFE and TAT. ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 98.76pt, "Regarding the PFE mechanism, it is reasonable to observe it ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 110.4pt, "at high temperatures and high electric fields, since the traps ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 122.04pt, "involved are deep (with energies of 0.75 eV and 0.9 eV) and ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 133.8pt, "electrons require sufficient thermal energy to escape from ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 145.44pt, "these traps. These deep traps are generally associated with ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 157.08pt, "nitrogen vacancies [18,19]. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.358pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(68.52pt, 179.16pt, "4. Conclusions  ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 9.345pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(79.32pt, 197.4pt, "For the sapphire-substrate sample, both Poole–Frenkel ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 209.16pt, "emission (PFE) and trap-assisted tunneling (TAT) are ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 220.8pt, "observed. At high temperatures and high electric fields, PFE ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 232.32pt, "dominates with a trap energy of 0.9 eV, whereas at lower ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 244.08pt, "temperatures and lower fields, TAT is the dominant ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 255.72pt, "mechanism with 0.29 eV. In contrast, for the GaN-substrate ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 267.48pt, "sample, only PFE is observed, with a trap energy of ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 279.12pt, "approximately 0.75 eV. This difference between the samples ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 290.76pt, "may be attributed to the significantly lower dislocation density ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 302.4pt, "and reduced defect concentration in the GaN substrate, which ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 314.04pt, "suppresses the contribution of tunneling-assisted mechanisms ")
  #line-at(68.52pt, 325.8pt, "and results in a single dominant PFE process. ")
